# Mobile API configuration.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and set the two values below. Expo inlines
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` variables at bundle time, so restart Metro with a cleared
# cache after editing: `npx expo start -c`.
#
# The phone (a native app) is NOT a browser, so it does not use the web app's
# Vite proxy and CORS does not apply: it needs an absolute URL that the phone
# itself can reach, including the backend. Pick one of the options below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option A - Same Wi-Fi (simplest). Phone and PC on the same network.
#   1. Find this PC's LAN IP:  ipconfig | findstr IPv4
#      (the backend also prints it at startup: "Reachable on your LAN: ...")
#   2. Use that IP for both values.
#   3. Allow the backend through the firewall. Windows classifies most Wi-Fi
#      networks as "Public" and blocks inbound connections by default, which
#      makes the phone hang until the request times out. Run this ONCE from an
#      elevated PowerShell:
#        New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName "SmartSchool Expo (TCP 4000)" `
#          -Direction Inbound -Action Allow -Protocol TCP -LocalPort 4000 `
#          -Profile Private,Public -RemoteAddress LocalSubnet
#        New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName "SmartSchool Expo (TCP 8081)" `
#          -Direction Inbound -Action Allow -Protocol TCP -LocalPort 8081 `
#          -Profile Private,Public -RemoteAddress LocalSubnet
#      Never use `localhost` here: on a physical phone it points at the phone
#      itself, not at the development machine.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://192.168.1.10:4000/api/v1
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL=http://192.168.1.10:4000
#
# Option B - USB + adb reverse. Phone and PC need not share a network.
#   1. Connect the phone over USB and enable USB debugging.
#   2. adb reverse tcp:8081 tcp:8081   (Metro)
#      adb reverse tcp:4000 tcp:4000   (backend)
#   3. Use localhost below and start Metro in localhost mode:
#      npx expo start --localhost
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://localhost:4000/api/v1
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL=http://localhost:4000
#
# Option C - Tunnels (phone is on a different network, no USB).
#   `npx expo start --tunnel` only tunnels Metro (the JS bundle); it does NOT
#   expose the backend. Tunnel the API as well and point the values at the
#   public https URL, e.g.:
#     npx cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:4000
#   then:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://<your-tunnel>.trycloudflare.com/api/v1
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL=https://<your-tunnel>.trycloudflare.com
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://10.245.90.244:4000/api/v1
EXPO_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL=http://10.245.90.244:4000
EXPO_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=true
